repository-code: "https://github.com/christina-18/qubofs"
abstract: >-
  quboFS is a classifier-independent Quadratic Unconstrained
  Binary Optimization (QUBO) feature-selection framework that
  jointly optimises gene-level relevance, pairwise non-redundancy
  and panel size to build compact, low-redundancy candidate
  biomarker panels from single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq)
  pseudobulk data. Relevance is the edgeR statistic weighted by
  cross-cohort consistency, computed on training donors only, and
  per-cell-type panels are combined by a cell-type-weighted soft
  vote. In leak-free nested cross-validation on four public
  cerebrospinal-fluid scRNA-seq cohorts for multiple sclerosis,
  and in two blood cohorts, quboFS produced the least-redundant
  panels among the evaluated methods with comparable held-out
  discrimination.
keywords:
  - multiple sclerosis
  - single-cell RNA sequencing
  - QUBO
  - gene panel selection
  - feature selection
  - within-panel redundancy
  - cohort-consistency weighting
  - cross-cohort validation
  - leave-one-cohort-out
  - nested cross-validation
